summary:
  The level watch files an answer that belongs to the previous group.

history:
  Measured 2026-09-20: the config held 30 while the listener had kept the
  room at 40 with the volume keys all evening. The only writer of the level
  was the disable's ack, and a panel restart or a reboot destroys the engine
  before that ack lands, so the next enable ramped back to a room close to
  inaudible. The level is now read every half minute while the room is
  alive — which makes the answer's guards the whole of its safety: a verify
  parks the master at 100, the ramp climbs through levels nobody chose, and
  a new generation starts at a polite 20.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
                  && parseInt(cmd.split(" ")[2], 10) === _combineLoadSeq)

replace:
                  && parseInt(cmd.split(" ")[2], 10) === parseInt(cmd.split(" ")[2], 10))

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine::test_a_watch_from_the_previous_generation_is_dropped.
  Line-neutral.
